Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:30:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zero-copy: the virglrenderer patch this branch needs, and
 what it does

contrib/qemu-gui/virglrenderer/ carries the virglrenderer patch that adds
virgl_renderer_resource_set_guest_dmabuf(), from the same DRM native
context work. qemu-gui-manager's File > Build QEMU applies the *.patch
files of that folder, after its own, to the virglrenderer it builds for
the branch; master has no such folder. The patch sums the iovecs itself,
so that it builds on virglrenderer 1.3.0 and main alike.

The README says what the branch does, what it needs on the host and in
the guest, and why it is a branch: pinned pages, guest kernel behaviour
upstream may change, and a virglrenderer call upstream will likely
replace with VIRTIO_GPU_F_CREATE_GUEST_HANDLE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
